1
00:00:16,708 --> 00:00:18,665
Help! Someone!

2
00:00:18,666 --> 00:00:20,750
[panting]

3
00:00:22,333 --> 00:00:23,166
[grunts]

4
00:00:24,083 --> 00:00:25,082
[groans]

5
00:00:25,083 --> 00:00:26,250
[exhales]

6
00:00:31,208 --> 00:00:32,124
Hey!

7
00:00:32,125 --> 00:00:34,040
Hold on. Mister!

8
00:00:34,041 --> 00:00:35,458
Hey, don't go!

9
00:00:35,958 --> 00:00:37,958
[tense music playing]

10
00:00:40,666 --> 00:00:42,332
[boy] Mister!

11
00:00:42,333 --> 00:00:44,416
[orchestral music playing in earphones]

12
00:00:45,541 --> 00:00:47,541
[boy panting]

13
00:00:48,583 --> 00:00:50,666
Please! Mister!

14
00:00:51,625 --> 00:00:53,625
[boy breathing heavily]

15
00:00:55,958 --> 00:00:56,791
Please help.

16
00:00:57,666 --> 00:00:58,791
It's my mom.

17
00:01:04,333 --> 00:01:05,791
[boy] <i>Please save my mom.</i>

18
00:01:07,541 --> 00:01:08,916
[phone alarm ringing]

19
00:01:10,708 --> 00:01:11,625
[grunts softly]

20
00:01:12,583 --> 00:01:13,416
[ringing stops]

21
00:01:16,875 --> 00:01:17,708
[laryngoscope thuds]

22
00:01:32,666 --> 00:01:34,915
You're not cut out for the emergency ward.

23
00:01:34,916 --> 00:01:37,832
You noticed the problem
on a patient's X-ray? Good job.

24
00:01:37,833 --> 00:01:41,875
But an emergency physician will face
critically ill patients every single day.

25
00:01:42,458 --> 00:01:44,458
It's not possible to save them all.

26
00:01:45,291 --> 00:01:46,833
So you can improve or leave.

27
00:01:47,958 --> 00:01:49,333
Tell me what you decide.

28
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:51,499
[footsteps receding]

29
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:53,583
[pensive music playing]

30
00:01:55,916 --> 00:01:59,375
CORE CASE ANALYSIS FOR ER PGY TRAINING

31
00:02:02,958 --> 00:02:04,291
ANATOMY FOR PHYSICIANS

32
00:02:08,208 --> 00:02:09,041
[exhales]

33
00:02:13,291 --> 00:02:15,458
[breathes deeply]

34
00:02:18,166 --> 00:02:19,457
[exhales]

35
00:02:19,458 --> 00:02:20,541
[sniffles]

36
00:02:22,250 --> 00:02:24,250
[opening theme music playing]

37
00:02:51,333 --> 00:02:52,707
MIRACLES OF THE ER

38
00:02:52,708 --> 00:02:55,083
EPISODE 2: ROOM FOR ERROR

39
00:02:57,166 --> 00:02:59,249
YANG-DA UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

40
00:02:59,250 --> 00:03:01,124
EMERGENCY DEPARTMENT

41
00:03:01,125 --> 00:03:02,499
- [woman] Can you direct me?
- Mmm-hmm.

42
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:04,708
- Right down the hall, to the left. Yep.
- [woman] Oh, thanks.

43
00:03:06,125 --> 00:03:06,957
Morning.

44
00:03:06,958 --> 00:03:07,875
Hmm?

45
00:03:09,208 --> 00:03:10,708
Iced milk tea, huh?

46
00:03:11,666 --> 00:03:13,125
Where is everyone?

47
00:03:13,708 --> 00:03:14,540
[sighs]

48
00:03:14,541 --> 00:03:16,665
That website was spot on.

49
00:03:16,666 --> 00:03:19,332
Cancer signs have bad luck today.

50
00:03:19,333 --> 00:03:22,040
[light music playing]

51
00:03:22,041 --> 00:03:23,165
What do you mean?

52
00:03:23,166 --> 00:03:24,083
What day is it?

53
00:03:24,666 --> 00:03:25,541
It's Friday.

54
00:03:26,125 --> 00:03:26,957
So that means...

55
00:03:26,958 --> 00:03:27,875
Well?

56
00:03:29,375 --> 00:03:30,624
- [yelps]
- [gasps]

57
00:03:30,625 --> 00:03:31,791
[Geng-ming] Morning meeting!

58
00:03:34,958 --> 00:03:36,165
And lastly,

59
00:03:36,166 --> 00:03:38,457
40-year-old male, persistent high fever.

60
00:03:38,458 --> 00:03:39,832
Generally weak and nauseous.

61
00:03:39,833 --> 00:03:41,957
Experiencing respiratory distress.

62
00:03:41,958 --> 00:03:43,290
So, what's going on here?

63
00:03:43,291 --> 00:03:46,457
Let's take a look at the records
and consider possible causes.

64
00:03:46,458 --> 00:03:48,166
TANG HSI

65
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:51,583
[Shao-ching] The R1 who's late...

66
00:03:53,041 --> 00:03:55,207
Why don't you give us your diagnosis?

67
00:03:55,208 --> 00:03:56,333
[exhales]

68
00:03:57,333 --> 00:03:58,166
Um...

69
00:03:59,916 --> 00:04:01,915
[mumbling] Respiratory distress.

70
00:04:01,916 --> 00:04:03,790
It takes you that long?

71
00:04:03,791 --> 00:04:06,125
You've got the medical records
and the test reports.

72
00:04:06,708 --> 00:04:08,165
The patient's condition deteriorated

73
00:04:08,166 --> 00:04:10,665
along with the onset
of respiratory distress.

74
00:04:10,666 --> 00:04:12,083
It's not obvious to you?

75
00:04:13,083 --> 00:04:15,791
Do you have some kind of problem
with communication?

76
00:04:17,583 --> 00:04:19,416
I'm sorry, I don't know.

77
00:04:19,916 --> 00:04:21,249
[doctors exclaim]

78
00:04:21,250 --> 00:04:22,333
[groans wearily]

79
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:27,665
Doctor Chiang,

80
00:04:27,666 --> 00:04:30,000
could you give us your diagnosis?

81
00:04:32,583 --> 00:04:33,666
KP.

82
00:04:34,250 --> 00:04:36,624
First of all, this man has diabetes

83
00:04:36,625 --> 00:04:38,499
and has developed multiple infections.

84
00:04:38,500 --> 00:04:40,332
He has pulmonary embolism.

85
00:04:40,333 --> 00:04:43,083
The chance
of bacterial thrombosis is high.

86
00:04:43,750 --> 00:04:44,707
He's presenting

87
00:04:44,708 --> 00:04:47,999
the classic characteristics
you'd see in a diabetic

88
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:49,791
with Klebsiella pneumoniae.

89
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,083
Excellent.

90
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:57,125
Yang-Da ER has always admitted elites.

91
00:04:57,791 --> 00:05:01,415
So if those with a low level of competence
want to join through connections,

92
00:05:01,416 --> 00:05:03,583
I suggest you work hard.

93
00:05:04,375 --> 00:05:06,915
As it turns out,
I've written several papers on KP.

94
00:05:06,916 --> 00:05:08,749
Read them when you have the time.

95
00:05:08,750 --> 00:05:10,250
We'll leave the morning meeting there.

96
00:05:13,375 --> 00:05:15,957
Hold on,
I need to check if you're a robot.

97
00:05:15,958 --> 00:05:17,332
Let's see here.

98
00:05:17,333 --> 00:05:18,624
His skin is warm.

99
00:05:18,625 --> 00:05:22,000
Well, thank you, God,
we got another genius R1.

100
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:25,249
- Come on, I'll buy you a coffee.
- [Tung-yen] Have you washed your hands?

101
00:05:25,250 --> 00:05:27,541
[Chih-cheng] Oh,
you're worried about my germs?

102
00:05:29,875 --> 00:05:30,708
Yu-hua.

103
00:05:31,583 --> 00:05:32,749
Meeting went well?

104
00:05:32,750 --> 00:05:33,665
[scoffs]

105
00:05:33,666 --> 00:05:36,791
Well, Dr. Cheng had a lot to say
to the new recruits.

106
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:38,790
[sighs]

107
00:05:38,791 --> 00:05:42,249
He always finds something to pick on
to make himself feel superior.

108
00:05:42,250 --> 00:05:43,375
Uh-huh.

109
00:05:45,708 --> 00:05:47,875
But one thing is different this year.

110
00:05:48,541 --> 00:05:52,416
I've never seen an R1
admit his mistakes so enthusiastically.

111
00:05:53,208 --> 00:05:54,125
Which one?

112
00:05:55,375 --> 00:05:56,250
Hmm.

113
00:05:56,875 --> 00:05:58,750
The bottom-ranked guy you picked.

114
00:06:00,083 --> 00:06:01,750
[sighs] Well, see ya.

115
00:06:08,625 --> 00:06:10,000
[inhales]

116
00:06:11,083 --> 00:06:12,208
[Geng-ming] Dr. Chou.

117
00:06:13,166 --> 00:06:14,625
Thank you for the materials.

118
00:06:17,541 --> 00:06:18,458
I'll get better.

119
00:06:20,666 --> 00:06:21,791
I want to be here.

120
00:06:27,166 --> 00:06:28,415
Email.

121
00:06:28,416 --> 00:06:29,500
Oh.

122
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:33,750
[lighthearted music playing]

123
00:06:38,333 --> 00:06:40,165
- Tell me when you've finished those.
- [phone buzzes]

124
00:06:40,166 --> 00:06:41,166
Oh. Ah...

125
00:06:45,125 --> 00:06:46,207
Oh, that's a lot.

126
00:06:46,208 --> 00:06:47,582
Is there a problem?

127
00:06:47,583 --> 00:06:49,750
Uh, it's fine.

128
00:06:50,875 --> 00:06:53,250
Get moving. Don't just stand there.

129
00:06:57,416 --> 00:06:58,749
[man breathes deeply]

130
00:06:58,750 --> 00:07:00,000
BEDS 06-11, 12-13

131
00:07:01,375 --> 00:07:02,750
[clears throat]

132
00:07:04,750 --> 00:07:07,375
- [exclaims] Mr. Chen, how are you feeling?
- [Chia-hao coughing]

133
00:07:08,416 --> 00:07:11,040
He has a fever that won't seem to go away.

134
00:07:11,041 --> 00:07:12,958
That's why we came to Emergency.

135
00:07:13,958 --> 00:07:15,832
37.8.

136
00:07:15,833 --> 00:07:16,916
Not too bad.

137
00:07:17,750 --> 00:07:19,957
And apart from coughing,
any other symptoms?

138
00:07:19,958 --> 00:07:21,624
Runny nose, sore throat?

139
00:07:21,625 --> 00:07:23,333
I've noticed both those things.

140
00:07:24,666 --> 00:07:26,415
Upper respiratory infection.

141
00:07:26,416 --> 00:07:27,749
I'll prescribe something.

142
00:07:27,750 --> 00:07:30,375
Drink water and avoid fatty food.
That's it.

143
00:07:31,125 --> 00:07:32,540
Not an IV drip or something?

144
00:07:32,541 --> 00:07:34,708
His fever keeps coming back.

145
00:07:35,375 --> 00:07:37,333
- [breathes raggedly]
- [Geng-ming] An IV drip?

146
00:07:38,208 --> 00:07:40,957
Sure. I'll get the nurse to give him one.

147
00:07:40,958 --> 00:07:43,957
- We'll observe him 'til the fever ends.
- Oh, okay, thanks.

148
00:07:43,958 --> 00:07:45,541
[breathing heavily]

149
00:07:46,208 --> 00:07:47,290
[exhales]

150
00:07:47,291 --> 00:07:49,582
Now type up the report
for the attending physician.

151
00:07:49,583 --> 00:07:50,500
Good. Okay.

152
00:07:51,625 --> 00:07:53,540
Bed passing through. Careful.

153
00:07:53,541 --> 00:07:55,832
I'm sorry, sir, but these are all steps...

154
00:07:55,833 --> 00:07:58,332
Come on, we've been here forever.

155
00:07:58,333 --> 00:08:00,499
- My tummy hurts a lot.
- [Hsiu-ju] All right, bed's here.

156
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:01,457
Oh god.

157
00:08:01,458 --> 00:08:03,707
- [man 2] Here, here.
- Come on, what is this place?

158
00:08:03,708 --> 00:08:05,374
- Leave me alone.
- [man 2] You took your time.

159
00:08:05,375 --> 00:08:07,332
- [Hsiu-ju] Okay, careful. Careful.
- What a bitch.

160
00:08:07,333 --> 00:08:08,290
[Tung-yen] Excuse me.

161
00:08:08,291 --> 00:08:10,915
- [patient] I wanna take off my shoes.
- Please mind your language.

162
00:08:10,916 --> 00:08:12,207
You're a doctor?

163
00:08:12,208 --> 00:08:14,874
Uh, we're here because my friend

164
00:08:14,875 --> 00:08:17,040
has a stomachache, and she's drunk.

165
00:08:17,041 --> 00:08:19,207
- That's the way.
- [man 2] Her back hurts, she said.

166
00:08:19,208 --> 00:08:20,915
- [patient] Mmm-hmm.
- No, thanks. No, thanks.

167
00:08:20,916 --> 00:08:21,832
[man 1 chuckles]

168
00:08:21,833 --> 00:08:22,999
- Hsiu-ju.
- Yeah?

169
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:24,582
[Tung-yen] Get a blood test
from her later.

170
00:08:24,583 --> 00:08:25,832
- Okay.
- [patient chuckling]

171
00:08:25,833 --> 00:08:27,332
Are you two her family?

172
00:08:27,333 --> 00:08:28,582
We need some details.

173
00:08:28,583 --> 00:08:30,832
- [groans]
- We're her friends.

174
00:08:30,833 --> 00:08:32,582
[patient chuckling]

175
00:08:32,583 --> 00:08:33,749
Well, stay here for me, okay?

176
00:08:33,750 --> 00:08:35,832
- [man 2] Uh-huh.
- [Hsiu-ju] Okay, come this way, please.

177
00:08:35,833 --> 00:08:39,207
Her name is Hsin-mei.
She turns up every few days.

178
00:08:39,208 --> 00:08:43,040
The test is going to show up
excessive alcohol consumption.

179
00:08:43,041 --> 00:08:44,625
Get used to it.

180
00:08:45,375 --> 00:08:47,375
[people chattering indistinctly]

181
00:08:50,750 --> 00:08:51,832
Hi, Doctor.

182
00:08:51,833 --> 00:08:53,249
Seen Dr. Chou around?

183
00:08:53,250 --> 00:08:55,916
I wanted to check
a management plan for a patient.

184
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:00,375
Uh... Oh.

185
00:09:02,708 --> 00:09:04,249
What's your plan, then?

186
00:09:04,250 --> 00:09:07,124
Hmm. The patient has a fever and a cough.

187
00:09:07,125 --> 00:09:10,540
I administered cold medication
and an IV drip.

188
00:09:10,541 --> 00:09:12,249
- That's all?
- Right.

189
00:09:12,250 --> 00:09:13,250
Blood sample?

190
00:09:14,291 --> 00:09:15,291
Uh, why?

191
00:09:16,250 --> 00:09:17,541
Breathing sound okay?

192
00:09:18,125 --> 00:09:19,040
I'm...

193
00:09:19,041 --> 00:09:20,082
not sure.

194
00:09:20,083 --> 00:09:22,916
[gasps] Why is his heart rate 140?

195
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:25,957
Don't know.

196
00:09:25,958 --> 00:09:28,041
[tense music playing]

197
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:32,249
He's recently had a splenectomy.

198
00:09:32,250 --> 00:09:33,624
His fever won't go down.

199
00:09:33,625 --> 00:09:36,499
But you ignored his heart rate
and didn't listen to his breath.

200
00:09:36,500 --> 00:09:38,999
You prescribed him cold medication.

201
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:40,332
Doctor.

202
00:09:40,333 --> 00:09:42,415
A man's life is in your hands.

203
00:09:42,416 --> 00:09:45,415
You can't leave things half done, okay?

204
00:09:45,416 --> 00:09:48,665
Uh, Doctor,
my husband's having trouble breathing.

205
00:09:48,666 --> 00:09:51,125
Can you check on him? He's gotten worse.

206
00:09:52,083 --> 00:09:54,083
[music swells]

207
00:09:56,125 --> 00:09:58,624
[Chia-hao breathing raggedly]

208
00:09:58,625 --> 00:10:00,125
[Yu-hua] Just wait here for now.

209
00:10:00,625 --> 00:10:02,624
Hsiu-ju, how long has he been like this?

210
00:10:02,625 --> 00:10:03,833
Few minutes now.

211
00:10:04,708 --> 00:10:06,708
[breathing heavily]

212
00:10:09,791 --> 00:10:11,082
Phlegm in both of his lungs.

213
00:10:11,083 --> 00:10:13,250
Geng-ming, what's your diagnosis?

214
00:10:13,875 --> 00:10:16,083
Uh, his saturation is quite low.

215
00:10:17,583 --> 00:10:18,582
Yeah, so?

216
00:10:18,583 --> 00:10:20,207
Give O2?

217
00:10:20,208 --> 00:10:22,208
- Hmm?
- O2!

218
00:10:22,791 --> 00:10:24,374
O2 mask, 10 liters.

219
00:10:24,375 --> 00:10:26,415
Check CBC, blood gas, and lactate.

220
00:10:26,416 --> 00:10:28,415
Blood culture, two sets, and an X-ray.

221
00:10:28,416 --> 00:10:29,332
[machine beeping]

222
00:10:29,333 --> 00:10:30,665
BP is getting low.

223
00:10:30,666 --> 00:10:33,624
- Saline challenge, 500.
- [coughing]

224
00:10:33,625 --> 00:10:34,957
- Go to Levophed.
- Is he...

225
00:10:34,958 --> 00:10:36,707
- Doctor...
- [Yu-hua] Stay back for me.

226
00:10:36,708 --> 00:10:38,832
Levophed. Let's do four at 500.

227
00:10:38,833 --> 00:10:40,457
- 20 cc and then another IV drip.
- Right.

228
00:10:40,458 --> 00:10:41,665
- Okay.
- Come.

229
00:10:41,666 --> 00:10:43,750
Why did things suddenly get so much worse?

230
00:10:44,250 --> 00:10:45,458
There is a chance of sepsis.

231
00:10:46,375 --> 00:10:48,875
We need to wait
for the test results to be certain.

232
00:10:49,500 --> 00:10:53,124
[breathes shakily]
But he... he told me it's just a cold.

233
00:10:53,125 --> 00:10:54,832
It's because of him. It's his fault.

234
00:10:54,833 --> 00:10:56,166
Now, Mrs. Chen.

235
00:10:57,208 --> 00:10:59,374
At the moment, there is a chance

236
00:10:59,375 --> 00:11:00,540
we'll need to intubate.

237
00:11:00,541 --> 00:11:02,499
[gasps] Could we not do that?

238
00:11:02,500 --> 00:11:04,374
Can you not intubate him, please?

239
00:11:04,375 --> 00:11:07,041
Because your husband
has had his spleen removed,

240
00:11:07,541 --> 00:11:10,207
there is a higher risk
of bacterial infection,

241
00:11:10,208 --> 00:11:12,540
particularly things like streptococci.

242
00:11:12,541 --> 00:11:14,957
Unfortunately, risk of mortality is high.

243
00:11:14,958 --> 00:11:16,624
[breathing heavily]

244
00:11:16,625 --> 00:11:19,332
No, please. You need to save him, Doctor.

245
00:11:19,333 --> 00:11:21,540
Save him. I'm begging you.

246
00:11:21,541 --> 00:11:23,624
We want the same thing, Mrs. Chen.

247
00:11:23,625 --> 00:11:26,207
- [sobbing]
- And I will do my best.

248
00:11:26,208 --> 00:11:28,499
But I'm not gonna lie.

249
00:11:28,500 --> 00:11:30,832
We need to be ready for anything.

250
00:11:30,833 --> 00:11:32,165
[Mrs. Chen] Okay.

251
00:11:32,166 --> 00:11:33,708
Do what you need to do.

252
00:11:34,583 --> 00:11:36,625
[sobbing] My god.

253
00:11:37,791 --> 00:11:39,165
[sobbing softly]

254
00:11:39,166 --> 00:11:41,541
[somber music playing]

255
00:11:45,166 --> 00:11:46,457
[exhales heavily]

256
00:11:46,458 --> 00:11:47,540
[inhales]

257
00:11:47,541 --> 00:11:48,833
What's up? You're stressed.

258
00:11:50,125 --> 00:11:51,207
I'll get straight to it.

259
00:11:51,208 --> 00:11:54,958
I don't know why you've chosen
Geng-ming to work here.

260
00:11:55,500 --> 00:11:57,083
He couldn't intubate, sure.

261
00:11:57,666 --> 00:11:59,915
But it's the second time now

262
00:11:59,916 --> 00:12:02,999
that he's failed
to give proper patient care.

263
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:04,749
[Hsiu-ju] That's true, Dr. Chou.

264
00:12:04,750 --> 00:12:06,874
We need talented R1s like Tung-yen.

265
00:12:06,875 --> 00:12:07,957
He's not on their level.

266
00:12:07,958 --> 00:12:10,332
I can't hold his hand for him.

267
00:12:10,333 --> 00:12:11,874
I'm a nurse, not your mama.

268
00:12:11,875 --> 00:12:13,457
[chuckles softly]

269
00:12:13,458 --> 00:12:14,540
[Chia-hsin] Hey, Cheng-chun.

270
00:12:14,541 --> 00:12:15,915
- [Cheng-chun] Yeah?
- I got you this.

271
00:12:15,916 --> 00:12:17,374
[Cheng-chun] Oh, thank you.

272
00:12:17,375 --> 00:12:19,582
Ah, sorry, did I interrupt you guys?

273
00:12:19,583 --> 00:12:21,500
- Oh, it's fine. How can I help?
- No.

274
00:12:22,125 --> 00:12:23,832
Actually, I'm here for Dr. He.

275
00:12:23,833 --> 00:12:24,875
[Cheng-chun] Oh.

276
00:12:25,583 --> 00:12:27,666
[Chia-hsin] Yu-hua, I was wondering if...

277
00:12:28,166 --> 00:12:31,915
we could discuss
the medical dispute mediation together.

278
00:12:31,916 --> 00:12:34,249
Ah. Oh, okay, yeah.

279
00:12:34,250 --> 00:12:35,250
- Hmm?
- Hmm.

280
00:12:47,458 --> 00:12:49,749
So, Yu-hua, I'll start with this.

281
00:12:49,750 --> 00:12:52,290
Yang-Da's position on litigation.

282
00:12:52,291 --> 00:12:55,540
It's always to be tactful
but also stand firm.

283
00:12:55,541 --> 00:12:58,124
This man's lost his wife. It's very sad.

284
00:12:58,125 --> 00:12:59,499
That's hard for him.

285
00:12:59,500 --> 00:13:02,665
But our doctors
are the heart of our work here.

286
00:13:02,666 --> 00:13:06,665
If the other party
tries damaging your reputation

287
00:13:06,666 --> 00:13:10,124
or wants to extort
large amounts of money from us,

288
00:13:10,125 --> 00:13:12,125
we will fight them all the way.

289
00:13:17,541 --> 00:13:19,208
What if I don't wanna fight?

290
00:13:21,875 --> 00:13:23,666
[panting]

291
00:13:28,250 --> 00:13:29,082
Oh my god.

292
00:13:29,083 --> 00:13:30,707
- Ugh, Mom.
- [Mrs. Yeh] Oh my.

293
00:13:30,708 --> 00:13:32,915
Why did you do this again?

294
00:13:32,916 --> 00:13:34,749
- I'm going home.
- What? No.

295
00:13:34,750 --> 00:13:36,832
- [Hsin-mei] Leave me alone, Mom.
- Excuse me.

296
00:13:36,833 --> 00:13:38,207
- What are you doing?
- Excuse me.

297
00:13:38,208 --> 00:13:40,457
I strongly recommend
you wait for test results.

298
00:13:40,458 --> 00:13:42,582
- There's a chance it's pancreatitis.
- No!

299
00:13:42,583 --> 00:13:43,874
- I'm going home.
- [grunting]

300
00:13:43,875 --> 00:13:45,041
- [retches]
- Oh!

301
00:13:46,833 --> 00:13:47,957
Oh...

302
00:13:47,958 --> 00:13:49,457
- Ah!
- Oh no.

303
00:13:49,458 --> 00:13:51,290
- Oh, dear.
- Ma'am, leave that to me.

304
00:13:51,291 --> 00:13:53,125
Huh? I'm sorry.

305
00:13:55,041 --> 00:13:56,915
- I'm so sorry. Sorry.
- [Geng-ming] No, it's fine.

306
00:13:56,916 --> 00:13:59,540
- [Hsin-mei] I'm going home.
- [Mrs. Yeh] Oh, come on, stand up.

307
00:13:59,541 --> 00:14:00,624
Come on.

308
00:14:00,625 --> 00:14:02,457
I do strongly recommend she stays.

309
00:14:02,458 --> 00:14:04,915
- [Hsin-mei] No! Going home!
- Okay, Hsin-mei.

310
00:14:04,916 --> 00:14:06,708
Okay, come home. Hurry.

311
00:14:08,083 --> 00:14:10,082
Hey, Tung-yen, wipe that up for me.

312
00:14:10,083 --> 00:14:12,041
- [Hsin-mei] I need to... [grunts]
- [Mrs. Yeh] Oh.

313
00:14:12,666 --> 00:14:14,875
- Hey! Excuse me, ma'am.
- [Mrs. Yeh] Come on.

314
00:14:21,500 --> 00:14:23,624
[Geng-ming] Excuse me.
Sorry, you forgot this.

315
00:14:23,625 --> 00:14:25,874
- [Mrs. Yeh] Oh.
- And be careful.

316
00:14:25,875 --> 00:14:27,540
- Make sure she drinks water.
- [Mrs. Yeh] Yes.

317
00:14:27,541 --> 00:14:29,707
[Geng-ming] And don't forget
to have plenty of rest.

318
00:14:29,708 --> 00:14:30,625
What's wrong?

319
00:14:31,833 --> 00:14:33,583
I got the patient's lab results.

320
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:37,165
Hey. Hey, look.

321
00:14:37,166 --> 00:14:38,374
[Hsiang-chun] Hmm?

322
00:14:38,375 --> 00:14:41,124
Amylase and lipase are both high.

323
00:14:41,125 --> 00:14:42,291
[gasps]

324
00:14:43,291 --> 00:14:45,624
- Acute pancreatitis.
- Mmm-hmm.

325
00:14:45,625 --> 00:14:47,499
- I wanted her to stay put.
- I can do it myself.

326
00:14:47,500 --> 00:14:50,124
[Tung-yen] But Geng-ming
just helped her out the door.

327
00:14:50,125 --> 00:14:52,082
[Mrs. Yeh] Don't worry. I'm your mom.

328
00:14:52,083 --> 00:14:53,583
[sighs]

329
00:14:58,708 --> 00:15:00,166
[inhales]

330
00:15:05,583 --> 00:15:06,458
[sighs]

331
00:15:07,833 --> 00:15:08,833
What do you want?

332
00:15:10,541 --> 00:15:12,791
Have I made you upset?

333
00:15:17,208 --> 00:15:19,999
That patient has pancreatitis.

334
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,207
But now we can't examine her.

335
00:15:22,208 --> 00:15:23,125
Well...

336
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:27,124
Well, I did see you didn't get them
to sign a voluntary discharge form.

337
00:15:27,125 --> 00:15:28,499
You must have been busy.

338
00:15:28,500 --> 00:15:31,290
But getting it signed retroactively
can be a real hassle.

339
00:15:31,291 --> 00:15:33,750
So I chased after them and got it.

340
00:15:35,750 --> 00:15:37,000
Worry about your own patients.

341
00:15:38,041 --> 00:15:39,291
[chopsticks thud]

342
00:15:45,791 --> 00:15:46,624
[phone beeps]

343
00:15:46,625 --> 00:15:48,874
ALL RECORDINGS, NEW RECORDING 14

344
00:15:48,875 --> 00:15:53,165
Mr. Yu, I'm the public relations director
for Yang-Da Hospital.

345
00:15:53,166 --> 00:15:54,707
My name's Chia-hsin.

346
00:15:54,708 --> 00:15:57,165
Will you be accompanied
by any family members

347
00:15:57,166 --> 00:15:58,916
or legal representatives today?

348
00:16:07,625 --> 00:16:09,707
- I just wanted to say--
- Great.

349
00:16:09,708 --> 00:16:11,041
Well, let's make a start.

350
00:16:13,166 --> 00:16:16,124
Yang-Da would like to convey
our deep remorse

351
00:16:16,125 --> 00:16:18,124
at what happened to your wife.

352
00:16:18,125 --> 00:16:20,415
But our investigation has shown

353
00:16:20,416 --> 00:16:23,916
there was no error of judgment
by the attending physician.

354
00:16:24,750 --> 00:16:26,082
Even so,

355
00:16:26,083 --> 00:16:28,874
we'd like to offer a sum of money
as a token of sympathy.

356
00:16:28,875 --> 00:16:30,333
We hope you'll accept.

357
00:16:31,625 --> 00:16:34,291
PAID TO: YU CHING-HSIANG, NT$100,000

358
00:16:36,125 --> 00:16:37,124
[inhales]

359
00:16:37,125 --> 00:16:38,624
[woman] Uh, there's a meeting in there.

360
00:16:38,625 --> 00:16:40,500
- [man] I'm the party involved.
- [door clanks]

361
00:16:42,875 --> 00:16:45,416
You started the meeting
without waiting for the lawyer?

362
00:16:45,916 --> 00:16:48,416
That's against procedure.
Right, Ms. Chang?

363
00:16:49,708 --> 00:16:52,291
Nice to see you again, Ms. Yang.

364
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:56,000
[tense music playing]

365
00:16:57,041 --> 00:16:58,665
That's all my sister's life is worth?

366
00:16:58,666 --> 00:17:00,249
This hospital is huge.

367
00:17:00,250 --> 00:17:02,457
How dare you try to fob us off?

368
00:17:02,458 --> 00:17:05,124
Ching-hsiang, I got us a lawyer.

369
00:17:05,125 --> 00:17:07,040
This hospital killed Yu-chuan.

370
00:17:07,041 --> 00:17:08,625
You can't let them get away with it.

371
00:17:09,208 --> 00:17:12,041
You don't need to worry.
The lawyer will handle everything.

372
00:17:12,625 --> 00:17:15,125
This family has been torn apart.

373
00:17:15,791 --> 00:17:18,625
And all Yang-Da can offer
is a pat on the head?

374
00:17:19,208 --> 00:17:20,916
My client will not accept that.

375
00:17:22,125 --> 00:17:24,916
Until you offer
more reasonable compensation,

376
00:17:26,166 --> 00:17:28,207
we'll be pursuing this case

377
00:17:28,208 --> 00:17:30,874
and the physician involved
to the very end.

378
00:17:30,875 --> 00:17:33,333
[music continues playing]

379
00:17:46,708 --> 00:17:47,750
[sighs heavily]

380
00:17:50,416 --> 00:17:51,500
[exhales]

381
00:17:57,208 --> 00:17:58,041
[sighs]

382
00:18:01,166 --> 00:18:02,791
[Yu-hua] This hospital is so big.

383
00:18:03,625 --> 00:18:06,791
Why is it so hard
to find a place to be alone?

384
00:18:07,791 --> 00:18:09,832
I started coming to the rooftop first.

385
00:18:09,833 --> 00:18:10,791
[sighs]

386
00:18:12,791 --> 00:18:14,375
Maybe you could lend it to me.

387
00:18:15,500 --> 00:18:16,500
For today.

388
00:18:17,375 --> 00:18:18,707
What's wrong?

389
00:18:18,708 --> 00:18:20,291
Mediation fell through?

390
00:18:23,125 --> 00:18:24,625
[sighs heavily]

391
00:18:25,916 --> 00:18:27,791
After everything that happened,

392
00:18:29,125 --> 00:18:31,041
seeing her husband looking like...

393
00:18:33,958 --> 00:18:36,000
like his whole life's been shattered.

394
00:18:37,041 --> 00:18:39,541
<i>Like he doesn't see the point
in living anymore.</i>

395
00:18:42,291 --> 00:18:43,415
I kept thinking,

396
00:18:43,416 --> 00:18:46,290
"What if I kept going?
What if I tried harder?"

397
00:18:46,291 --> 00:18:47,208
[exhales]

398
00:18:48,333 --> 00:18:49,958
Then we wouldn't be here.

399
00:18:50,875 --> 00:18:51,874
[Cheng-chun] Yu-hua.

400
00:18:51,875 --> 00:18:53,290
It wasn't your fault.

401
00:18:53,291 --> 00:18:54,999
[sighs]

402
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:56,833
[somber music playing]

403
00:18:58,958 --> 00:18:59,916
[sighs]

404
00:19:02,625 --> 00:19:04,541
I hope we never get numb

405
00:19:05,833 --> 00:19:07,375
to these sorts of feelings.

406
00:19:08,208 --> 00:19:09,125
You know?

407
00:19:15,875 --> 00:19:18,041
[breathes deeply]

408
00:19:27,250 --> 00:19:28,416
And show me.

409
00:19:29,166 --> 00:19:31,165
- Great. Ah, ma'am.
- Uh-huh?

410
00:19:31,166 --> 00:19:32,499
Stay here with your grandson,

411
00:19:32,500 --> 00:19:35,250
and I'll ask the doctor
to come over, okay?

412
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:38,124
Doctor, this patient has a cut.

413
00:19:38,125 --> 00:19:39,541
Here's his chart.

414
00:19:40,125 --> 00:19:43,415
Try to avoid giving new patients
just before handover.

415
00:19:43,416 --> 00:19:45,708
- Oh, well, I...
- Is this your first day as a nurse?

416
00:19:48,083 --> 00:19:49,166
Dr. Tang.

417
00:19:49,666 --> 00:19:50,583
Dr. Cheng?

418
00:19:51,208 --> 00:19:52,541
- There you go.
- Great.

419
00:19:57,583 --> 00:19:59,958
- This patient has a laceration.
- [Hsi] Mmm-hmm.

420
00:20:00,958 --> 00:20:02,875
[patient] Uh, I've got a bad headache.

421
00:20:06,916 --> 00:20:08,124
Where does it hurt?

422
00:20:08,125 --> 00:20:11,332
I think my grandson was bitten by a dog.

423
00:20:11,333 --> 00:20:13,541
All right. Let me check his wound, then.

424
00:20:15,833 --> 00:20:17,166
It looks quite deep.

425
00:20:18,416 --> 00:20:20,124
And when did this happen?

426
00:20:20,125 --> 00:20:21,791
[groans] Does it matter?

427
00:20:22,291 --> 00:20:23,957
[Chun-ting's grandma] Uh, I'm sorry.

428
00:20:23,958 --> 00:20:28,624
I only noticed it when I woke him up
for breakfast this morning.

429
00:20:28,625 --> 00:20:30,040
Is it a bad one or...

430
00:20:30,041 --> 00:20:33,332
Uh... I'll give him a tetanus shot
and clean his wound.

431
00:20:33,333 --> 00:20:35,999
And then, he'll need to do
a round of antibiotics

432
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:38,374
and make sure the wound stays clean.

433
00:20:38,375 --> 00:20:40,499
Oh, that's a lot to do.

434
00:20:40,500 --> 00:20:42,250
Will that cost very much?

435
00:20:42,833 --> 00:20:44,582
Oh, it's covered by insurance.

436
00:20:44,583 --> 00:20:46,582
So it'll only be a few hundred.

437
00:20:46,583 --> 00:20:47,666
Oh.

438
00:20:48,458 --> 00:20:50,790
- It won't cost much money.
- [exclaims]

439
00:20:50,791 --> 00:20:53,415
Come and find me if you have questions.
My name is Tang Hsi.

440
00:20:53,416 --> 00:20:56,875
- Oh, Dr. Tang Hsi, I'm so grateful.
- [Hsi] Mmm-hmm.

441
00:20:58,125 --> 00:21:00,832
- Just keep your arm up here, okay?
- [Chun-ting's grandma] Yes, yes.

442
00:21:00,833 --> 00:21:03,415
- [Yuan-ting] Make sure you follow it up.
- [Hsiang-chun] Yeah, uh-huh.

443
00:21:03,416 --> 00:21:04,957
- For admission...
- [nurse 1] Hi, Dr. Huang.

444
00:21:04,958 --> 00:21:06,707
- ...you'll look down over here.
- [nurse 2] Hi.

445
00:21:06,708 --> 00:21:08,625
- [Hsiang-chun] Mmm-hmm.
- [Yuan-ting] You can see...

446
00:21:12,041 --> 00:21:13,290
It's Dr. Huang.

447
00:21:13,291 --> 00:21:15,041
He was on TV last night.

448
00:21:16,750 --> 00:21:18,165
Do your job.

449
00:21:18,166 --> 00:21:19,499
[Yuan-ting groans]

450
00:21:19,500 --> 00:21:21,083
[Hsiang-chun] Go on, back to work.

451
00:21:23,125 --> 00:21:25,082
Well, you've graced us here on earth.

452
00:21:25,083 --> 00:21:26,999
- [You-chang] Just for you.
- [Shao-ching] Oh.

453
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:29,125
[chuckles] Yu-hua around?

454
00:21:29,916 --> 00:21:31,666
Ah. Over there.

455
00:21:33,208 --> 00:21:35,416
I knew you weren't here to see me.

456
00:21:37,958 --> 00:21:39,624
- Doctor.
- Doctor.

457
00:21:39,625 --> 00:21:40,582
Can I?

458
00:21:40,583 --> 00:21:42,333
Okay. See you.

459
00:21:44,625 --> 00:21:45,666
Hmm.

460
00:21:46,916 --> 00:21:49,125
[softly] Did the mediation go well?

461
00:21:50,833 --> 00:21:51,750
Hmm.

462
00:21:55,125 --> 00:21:56,124
Let's go, then.

463
00:21:56,125 --> 00:21:57,875
I'll train with you. You can punch me.

464
00:21:59,083 --> 00:22:00,415
- I will.
- [chuckles]

465
00:22:00,416 --> 00:22:01,665
You've said I can now.

466
00:22:01,666 --> 00:22:05,166
- [You-chang laughs] Pick you up at 8:00?
- [Yu-hua] Mmm-hmm.

467
00:22:06,750 --> 00:22:09,332
And, Cheng, let's go for a meal next time.

468
00:22:09,333 --> 00:22:10,374
If you pay.

469
00:22:10,375 --> 00:22:11,625
[You-chang] Okay.

470
00:22:17,708 --> 00:22:19,290
[Shao-ching] Done with the patient?

471
00:22:19,291 --> 00:22:21,374
Hmm. If there's nothing else
that you'd like to add,

472
00:22:21,375 --> 00:22:22,290
I'll discharge him now.

473
00:22:22,291 --> 00:22:23,374
Right.

474
00:22:23,375 --> 00:22:25,624
Ah, just make sure the patient understands

475
00:22:25,625 --> 00:22:28,457
that if there's a fever
or there's swelling around the wound,

476
00:22:28,458 --> 00:22:29,915
he needs to come back at once.

477
00:22:29,916 --> 00:22:30,833
I've told him.

478
00:22:31,416 --> 00:22:32,250
Good.

479
00:22:35,375 --> 00:22:38,749
- Uh, I found this video the patient made.
- [Chun-ting yelling on phone]

480
00:22:38,750 --> 00:22:40,790
There's a possibility he's abusing dogs.

481
00:22:40,791 --> 00:22:43,999
Should I get in touch
with police or a social worker?

482
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:46,540
- Just over this? Don't get involved.
- [dog barking]

483
00:22:46,541 --> 00:22:49,332
- The kid's being a kid.
- [Chun-ting] <i>Take that. Fuck you.</i>

484
00:22:49,333 --> 00:22:50,916
[Shao-ching] You handled the patient well.

485
00:22:51,416 --> 00:22:54,041
So, if that's everything,
you can head home.

486
00:22:58,375 --> 00:23:00,707
I'll let you know when it's all confirmed.

487
00:23:00,708 --> 00:23:02,457
Hmm. Right.

488
00:23:02,458 --> 00:23:03,583
See you.

489
00:23:05,291 --> 00:23:06,874
- Cheng-chun, um...
- Hi.

490
00:23:06,875 --> 00:23:10,332
Someone called Wei Sung
was admitted to the ER yesterday.

491
00:23:10,333 --> 00:23:12,332
I wanted to check
which doctor intubated him.

492
00:23:12,333 --> 00:23:13,250
Is there a problem?

493
00:23:14,166 --> 00:23:17,624
His son seems unhappy
with how the intubation went.

494
00:23:17,625 --> 00:23:19,624
- He's asking for the medical records.
- Huh.

495
00:23:19,625 --> 00:23:21,416
- Uh, I'll check.
- [Chia-hsin] Thanks.

496
00:23:25,208 --> 00:23:27,333
[pensive music playing]

497
00:23:27,958 --> 00:23:28,791
[sighs]

498
00:23:29,416 --> 00:23:32,041
The doctors involved
were Yu-hua and Geng-ming.

499
00:23:33,916 --> 00:23:36,708
Oh, so it's Dr. Yu-hua once more.

500
00:23:37,291 --> 00:23:38,249
What's wrong?

501
00:23:38,250 --> 00:23:40,208
Did their mediation not go well?

502
00:23:41,208 --> 00:23:42,915
Are you asking because...

503
00:23:42,916 --> 00:23:45,874
you're worried about me and Yang-Da?

504
00:23:45,875 --> 00:23:47,125
Or about Yu-hua?

505
00:23:49,291 --> 00:23:50,125
Huh?

506
00:23:50,958 --> 00:23:52,541
It's not clear what I'm asking?

507
00:23:56,500 --> 00:23:59,375
Well, I'll follow up with Yu-hua.

508
00:24:00,083 --> 00:24:02,041
- Good night.
- [Cheng-chun] Bye.

509
00:24:07,666 --> 00:24:08,708
Don't want it?

510
00:24:09,541 --> 00:24:10,957
You know, if you're not interested,

511
00:24:10,958 --> 00:24:13,750
then don't accept what she offers you.

512
00:24:15,458 --> 00:24:17,665
You don't want a coffee? I'll drink it.

513
00:24:17,666 --> 00:24:19,750
[music continues playing]

514
00:24:23,708 --> 00:24:24,708
[scoffs]

515
00:24:25,375 --> 00:24:26,832
One, one. Two, two.

516
00:24:26,833 --> 00:24:27,749
Switch. Yeah.

517
00:24:27,750 --> 00:24:29,207
[both panting softly]

518
00:24:29,208 --> 00:24:30,291
Okay. Come on.

519
00:24:30,958 --> 00:24:31,791
One.

520
00:24:32,541 --> 00:24:35,540
One, two, three. One, two, three.

521
00:24:35,541 --> 00:24:36,957
Slip, slip, hook, yeah.

522
00:24:36,958 --> 00:24:39,958
Come on, come on.
One, two, one, one, yeah.

523
00:24:40,625 --> 00:24:42,625
[both panting]

524
00:24:44,041 --> 00:24:44,916
Yeah.

525
00:24:45,791 --> 00:24:47,374
- [grunts]
- One, two. One, two.

526
00:24:47,375 --> 00:24:48,957
One, two, slip. Yeah.

527
00:24:48,958 --> 00:24:50,374
- One, one, yeah.
- [grunting]

528
00:24:50,375 --> 00:24:52,707
- [grunts fiercely]
- Hey, hey, hey.

529
00:24:52,708 --> 00:24:54,082
Hey, hey. Okay. Hey!

530
00:24:54,083 --> 00:24:55,165
Okay, stop.

531
00:24:55,166 --> 00:24:57,707
[both breathing heavily]

532
00:24:57,708 --> 00:24:59,999
- [exhales]
<i>- I'm a good punching bag today, hey.</i>

533
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:01,125
[exhales]

534
00:25:02,208 --> 00:25:03,583
You're not bad.

535
00:25:04,958 --> 00:25:06,957
It's good to have a friend to beat up.

536
00:25:06,958 --> 00:25:08,750
- [laughs]
- [chuckles softly]

537
00:25:11,958 --> 00:25:13,125
How's your paper going?

538
00:25:13,875 --> 00:25:15,375
Hmm. Pretty well.

539
00:25:16,125 --> 00:25:18,125
I'm glad. [chuckles]

540
00:25:19,833 --> 00:25:22,040
I heard Dr. Chou's papers
on the same thing.

541
00:25:22,041 --> 00:25:23,124
[You-chang] Hmm.

542
00:25:23,125 --> 00:25:24,583
[inhales]

543
00:25:25,958 --> 00:25:29,291
We're now in human trials
for this lung cancer drug, Phase II.

544
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:33,791
And Director Chang just let Dr. Chou
use my word for his publication.

545
00:25:35,000 --> 00:25:36,166
Too much bias.

546
00:25:39,916 --> 00:25:41,000
[sighs]

547
00:25:42,166 --> 00:25:43,125
How about you?

548
00:25:43,750 --> 00:25:46,000
- Your research going well?
- [scoffs]

549
00:25:47,208 --> 00:25:48,499
It's going fine.

550
00:25:48,500 --> 00:25:50,249
And your promotion.

551
00:25:50,250 --> 00:25:52,290
You can't be
an attending physician forever.

552
00:25:52,291 --> 00:25:55,082
I get that this is how the system is.

553
00:25:55,083 --> 00:25:58,207
And I get that research papers
are important to the world,

554
00:25:58,208 --> 00:26:00,665
but don't you think
using them as the standard

555
00:26:00,666 --> 00:26:03,749
to evaluate a doctor's competence
is a bit unfair?

556
00:26:03,750 --> 00:26:08,041
Is a doctor who just saves people's lives
not worthy of promotion?

557
00:26:08,625 --> 00:26:09,790
[exhales]

558
00:26:09,791 --> 00:26:10,958
I've always said,

559
00:26:11,791 --> 00:26:14,166
I'd be happy to help
with your paper if you need.

560
00:26:15,166 --> 00:26:16,208
I know.

561
00:26:23,375 --> 00:26:25,458
[elevator bell dings]

562
00:26:30,458 --> 00:26:31,457
[Geng-ming] Hey!

563
00:26:31,458 --> 00:26:33,541
[soft music playing]

564
00:26:35,291 --> 00:26:37,083
- Do you live here?
- Mmm-hmm.

565
00:26:38,166 --> 00:26:39,166
[softly] Top floor?

566
00:26:40,083 --> 00:26:42,250
That's an expensive place. Wow.

567
00:26:44,125 --> 00:26:45,833
[elevator doors slide open]

568
00:26:50,708 --> 00:26:52,625
[elevator doors slide close]

569
00:26:53,291 --> 00:26:55,583
Are you still mad at me?

570
00:26:56,291 --> 00:26:58,374
[breathes deeply]

571
00:26:58,375 --> 00:26:59,458
So, Tung-yen,

572
00:27:00,083 --> 00:27:01,582
you're a first-honor graduate.

573
00:27:01,583 --> 00:27:04,708
If I need some advice on a patient,
would asking you be okay?

574
00:27:05,291 --> 00:27:09,082
Actually, I just recently encountered
a patient I'm really concerned about.

575
00:27:09,083 --> 00:27:10,375
[elevator doors slide open]

576
00:27:12,916 --> 00:27:16,040
He had a splenectomy
and went to ER with recurrent fevers.

577
00:27:16,041 --> 00:27:18,290
He's got a cough,
and there's phlegm in both lungs.

578
00:27:18,291 --> 00:27:21,874
It looks like your case of streptococci,
but he hasn't been abroad recently.

579
00:27:21,875 --> 00:27:23,082
What do you think is going on?

580
00:27:23,083 --> 00:27:24,916
[door closes]

581
00:27:26,000 --> 00:27:27,083
Huh.

582
00:27:27,750 --> 00:27:29,499
Nice to talk to you.

583
00:27:29,500 --> 00:27:30,416
Night.

584
00:27:32,833 --> 00:27:34,082
- Mom!
- [Mrs. Tang] Tang Hsi.

585
00:27:34,083 --> 00:27:37,457
Listen, your brother's really making
a big fuss over nothing.

586
00:27:37,458 --> 00:27:39,749
Dragging me all this way to get examined

587
00:27:39,750 --> 00:27:42,915
- when we all know how busy you are.
- All right.

588
00:27:42,916 --> 00:27:44,999
Now we're gonna... [coughs]

589
00:27:45,000 --> 00:27:47,040
- Mom.
- [coughing]

590
00:27:47,041 --> 00:27:48,915
- Do you need some water?
- [coughs loudly]

591
00:27:48,916 --> 00:27:51,415
- Why are you coughing like this?
- Mom, you okay?

592
00:27:51,416 --> 00:27:54,124
- I'm okay. I'll have some water later.
- Oh.

593
00:27:54,125 --> 00:27:56,374
You get back home. Beat the traffic.

594
00:27:56,375 --> 00:27:57,874
- Go, go.
- All right.

595
00:27:57,875 --> 00:28:01,040
- I'll head off, then.
- [coughs] I'll get some water.

596
00:28:01,041 --> 00:28:02,625
[coughing]

597
00:28:09,208 --> 00:28:10,500
It doesn't make sense.

598
00:28:11,208 --> 00:28:14,000
She was doing fine, and now it's back.

599
00:28:18,250 --> 00:28:19,708
Have you talked to your work?

600
00:28:20,291 --> 00:28:22,250
Yeah, they're making the arrangements.

601
00:28:24,375 --> 00:28:25,375
[sighs]

602
00:28:26,041 --> 00:28:27,916
Mom's gotten really thin lately.

603
00:28:28,500 --> 00:28:29,333
Hmm.

604
00:28:30,458 --> 00:28:31,457
Don't worry.

605
00:28:31,458 --> 00:28:34,957
I chose emergency medicine
for the fixed schedule to look after Mom.

606
00:28:34,958 --> 00:28:36,458
[Mrs. Tang coughing]

607
00:28:37,125 --> 00:28:38,749
- Okay, bye.
- You head off. Take care.

608
00:28:38,750 --> 00:28:40,624
- Okay.
- [coughing]

609
00:28:40,625 --> 00:28:42,749
Hey, drive safely.

610
00:28:42,750 --> 00:28:44,625
Yeah, I will. Bye-bye.

611
00:28:47,208 --> 00:28:48,125
[coughing]

612
00:28:48,708 --> 00:28:50,541
Mom, want some food?

613
00:28:52,250 --> 00:28:53,415
[Mrs. Tang] Darling.

614
00:28:53,416 --> 00:28:55,583
Now, be honest with me.

615
00:28:58,375 --> 00:28:59,290
Is it...

616
00:28:59,291 --> 00:29:01,208
Is it back again?

617
00:29:02,208 --> 00:29:03,291
[sighs]

618
00:29:06,500 --> 00:29:07,791
[Geng-ming exhales]

619
00:29:11,083 --> 00:29:11,916
[doorbell dings]

620
00:29:20,958 --> 00:29:21,916
[exclaims]

621
00:29:22,750 --> 00:29:24,874
Splenectomy followed by recurrent fever.

622
00:29:24,875 --> 00:29:27,832
Fulminant streptococcal infection
with ARDS.

623
00:29:27,833 --> 00:29:31,083
What's important is to find out
what caused the infection.

624
00:29:31,791 --> 00:29:34,500
[upbeat music playing]

625
00:29:35,166 --> 00:29:37,208
[stomach grumbles]

626
00:29:39,000 --> 00:29:39,915
That's all.

627
00:29:39,916 --> 00:29:41,082
[Geng-ming] Oh, thank you.

628
00:29:41,083 --> 00:29:42,165
Hey, hey, hey.

629
00:29:42,166 --> 00:29:44,500
The least I could do
is give you some food.

630
00:29:47,291 --> 00:29:48,291
Have you seen...

631
00:29:49,500 --> 00:29:51,249
[objects clattering]

632
00:29:51,250 --> 00:29:52,166
Here.

633
00:29:56,166 --> 00:29:57,000
Maybe...

634
00:29:58,583 --> 00:30:00,333
put on a pair of pants first?

635
00:30:03,250 --> 00:30:04,333
[Geng-ming] Oh, sure.

636
00:30:06,833 --> 00:30:09,500
YANG-DA UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

637
00:30:14,291 --> 00:30:17,041
[Geng-ming] Hi. Excuse me,
can I ask where's Chen Chia-hao?

638
00:30:17,625 --> 00:30:19,166
[nurse] Chen Chia-hao, I'll check.

639
00:30:19,750 --> 00:30:21,125
Currently preparing for surgery.

640
00:30:22,208 --> 00:30:23,290
[Geng-ming] Oh, what happened?

641
00:30:23,291 --> 00:30:25,666
[nurse] ICH and multiple brain abscesses.

642
00:30:27,166 --> 00:30:29,458
- [Geng-ming] Oh, thanks very much.
- [nurse] Hmm.

643
00:30:37,708 --> 00:30:39,915
[Geng-ming] Mrs. Chen, don't worry.

644
00:30:39,916 --> 00:30:42,583
I... I'll find the source
of the bacterial infection.

645
00:30:43,083 --> 00:30:45,749
[Mrs. Chen] Doctor,
please stop pretending it's all okay.

646
00:30:45,750 --> 00:30:48,415
Chia-hao wouldn't be like this
if it wasn't for you.

647
00:30:48,416 --> 00:30:50,165
[sobbing]

648
00:30:50,166 --> 00:30:52,750
[somber music playing]

649
00:31:02,500 --> 00:31:04,124
DOCTOR: HUANG YOU-CHANG

650
00:31:04,125 --> 00:31:05,957
[You-chang] You're Yu-hua's junior doctor?

651
00:31:05,958 --> 00:31:06,999
Right.

652
00:31:07,000 --> 00:31:09,124
She's fierce when she's working.

653
00:31:09,125 --> 00:31:11,249
Oh, I've actually learned a lot from her.

654
00:31:11,250 --> 00:31:14,333
[chuckles] You can be honest with me.
I won't tell on you.

655
00:31:15,000 --> 00:31:16,249
[chuckles]

656
00:31:16,250 --> 00:31:17,582
All right.

657
00:31:17,583 --> 00:31:19,999
So, I've received
your pathology and your imaging,

658
00:31:20,000 --> 00:31:21,499
and I'm aware of the situation.

659
00:31:21,500 --> 00:31:23,707
So now there's just a few more tests left,

660
00:31:23,708 --> 00:31:27,415
and we can evaluate which treatment method
will be best moving forward.

661
00:31:27,416 --> 00:31:28,332
Ah.

662
00:31:28,333 --> 00:31:30,290
- [Mrs. Tang coughs]
- Doctor.

663
00:31:30,291 --> 00:31:31,374
I've heard at Yang-Da

664
00:31:31,375 --> 00:31:33,666
there's a clinical trial
for a new cancer drug.

665
00:31:34,250 --> 00:31:37,415
From what I could see, it looks like
there aren't many side effects,

666
00:31:37,416 --> 00:31:41,499
and it works quite well
without impacting the patient very much.

667
00:31:41,500 --> 00:31:44,999
I wonder if there's a chance
we could join the trial.

668
00:31:45,000 --> 00:31:46,540
[inhales]

669
00:31:46,541 --> 00:31:48,083
[You-chang] Mmm...

670
00:31:49,166 --> 00:31:50,250
I'm...

671
00:31:50,916 --> 00:31:51,750
I'm very sorry.

672
00:31:52,375 --> 00:31:54,208
There are no more slots
for that trial left.

673
00:31:55,083 --> 00:31:57,374
I'll look for other treatment options
for your mom.

674
00:31:57,375 --> 00:31:58,540
[Mrs. Tang coughing]

675
00:31:58,541 --> 00:31:59,874
Let's get her admitted first up.

676
00:31:59,875 --> 00:32:01,040
Mmm-hmm.

677
00:32:01,041 --> 00:32:02,374
[Mrs. Tang coughing]

678
00:32:02,375 --> 00:32:04,166
[siren wailing]

679
00:32:06,166 --> 00:32:08,124
- All right, coming through!
- [Chih-kai] Coming through.

680
00:32:08,125 --> 00:32:09,165
Dr. Chou!

681
00:32:09,166 --> 00:32:10,874
OHCA! Hurry.

682
00:32:10,875 --> 00:32:13,083
- Resus Room 1.
- [Hsiu-ju] Quickly, quickly.

683
00:32:13,666 --> 00:32:16,457
She was in here before
with acute pancreatitis.

684
00:32:16,458 --> 00:32:18,416
[suspenseful music playing]

685
00:32:19,875 --> 00:32:20,915
On my call. One, two...

686
00:32:20,916 --> 00:32:21,916
- Three.
- Three.

687
00:32:23,416 --> 00:32:24,290
What happened here?

688
00:32:24,291 --> 00:32:27,082
[Chih-kai] Wasn't breathing,
had no heartbeat when we arrived.

689
00:32:27,083 --> 00:32:28,582
AED didn't recommend defib.

690
00:32:28,583 --> 00:32:30,082
We did CPR all the way here.

691
00:32:30,083 --> 00:32:31,582
[Hsiu-ju panting]

692
00:32:31,583 --> 00:32:33,082
I'll leave her to you.

693
00:32:33,083 --> 00:32:34,791
[panting]

694
00:32:36,250 --> 00:32:37,749
It's Hsin-mei.

695
00:32:37,750 --> 00:32:38,749
- Geng-ming.
- Yeah?

696
00:32:38,750 --> 00:32:40,790
- Take over compressions.
- Uh-huh.

697
00:32:40,791 --> 00:32:42,665
[Hsiu-ju] Three, two, one.

698
00:32:42,666 --> 00:32:44,957
[Cheng-chun] Patient with OHCA,
what do we do first?

699
00:32:44,958 --> 00:32:47,290
[Geng-ming] Intubate
to restore vital signs, then ICU.

700
00:32:47,291 --> 00:32:48,374
- Hsiu-ju.
- [Hsiu-ju] Doctor.

701
00:32:48,375 --> 00:32:50,165
- Epi, one every three minutes.
- Right, got it.

702
00:32:50,166 --> 00:32:52,083
- Su-ching, get a tube.
- [Su-ching] Right.

703
00:32:54,500 --> 00:32:56,125
[music continues playing]

704
00:32:58,541 --> 00:32:59,875
First dose of epi is done now.

705
00:33:09,208 --> 00:33:10,207
Hold compressions.

706
00:33:10,208 --> 00:33:12,082
[machine emits a long beep]

707
00:33:12,083 --> 00:33:13,165
Good, continue.

708
00:33:13,166 --> 00:33:15,250
[machine beeping]

709
00:33:20,166 --> 00:33:21,207
Right, step away.

710
00:33:21,208 --> 00:33:22,790
[machine emits a long beep]

711
00:33:22,791 --> 00:33:23,874
[panting]

712
00:33:23,875 --> 00:33:24,791
Okay.

713
00:33:27,625 --> 00:33:29,625
[Mrs. Yeh sniffling, sobbing softly]

714
00:33:37,791 --> 00:33:39,791
[long beep continues]

715
00:33:46,958 --> 00:33:48,916
- [Cheng-chun] Resume compressions.
- [Geng-ming] Right.

716
00:33:51,375 --> 00:33:53,500
[Hsiu-ju] Mrs. Yeh, please have a seat.

717
00:33:55,791 --> 00:33:57,916
[panting]

718
00:33:59,250 --> 00:34:00,500
Your mom's waiting.

719
00:34:01,416 --> 00:34:02,625
You can't give up.

720
00:34:04,916 --> 00:34:06,916
[Cheng-chun] Time's up.
Inject the second one.

721
00:34:08,375 --> 00:34:10,625
[machine beeping]

722
00:34:23,666 --> 00:34:25,666
[ominous music playing]

723
00:34:31,500 --> 00:34:33,708
[Geng-ming panting]

724
00:34:37,500 --> 00:34:40,332
Epi, last dose.
We're 30 minutes into resus now.

725
00:34:40,333 --> 00:34:41,790
[Geng-ming panting]

726
00:34:41,791 --> 00:34:44,125
[machine emits a long beep]

727
00:34:45,916 --> 00:34:46,916
No pulse.

728
00:34:48,125 --> 00:34:49,666
Hsiu-ju, bring the family in, please.

729
00:34:50,250 --> 00:34:51,916
- Uh-huh.
- [Geng-ming panting]

730
00:34:53,708 --> 00:34:56,833
Mrs. Yeh, the physician's asked you
to come through, please.

731
00:35:00,583 --> 00:35:02,083
[Geng-ming panting]

732
00:35:03,250 --> 00:35:04,375
[Cheng-chun] Mrs. Yeh.

733
00:35:05,083 --> 00:35:07,207
We were unable to resuscitate.

734
00:35:07,208 --> 00:35:08,625
Unfortunately.

735
00:35:09,416 --> 00:35:12,041
At this point,
we need to ease her suffering.

736
00:35:16,041 --> 00:35:18,041
[Geng-ming panting]

737
00:35:20,250 --> 00:35:21,458
- [sobs]
- Geng-ming.

738
00:35:22,041 --> 00:35:23,999
[machine emits a long beep]

739
00:35:24,000 --> 00:35:26,040
Time of death, 10:11 a.m.

740
00:35:26,041 --> 00:35:26,957
I'm sorry.

741
00:35:26,958 --> 00:35:29,041
[somber music playing]

742
00:35:30,791 --> 00:35:32,791
[breath trembling]

743
00:35:33,875 --> 00:35:36,082
[whimpers] Hsin-mei...

744
00:35:36,083 --> 00:35:38,958
[sobbing] My girl.

745
00:35:40,666 --> 00:35:42,541
Hsin-mei.

746
00:35:43,041 --> 00:35:44,124
My...

747
00:35:44,125 --> 00:35:46,166
[sobbing]

748
00:35:47,041 --> 00:35:49,832
Mama's calling you. Answer me!

749
00:35:49,833 --> 00:35:52,250
Oh, my girl.

750
00:35:56,291 --> 00:35:58,583
Hsin-mei... [wailing]

751
00:36:02,541 --> 00:36:04,416
[sobbing]

752
00:36:09,375 --> 00:36:11,415
Hsin-mei!

753
00:36:11,416 --> 00:36:13,666
[wailing loudly]

754
00:36:24,291 --> 00:36:25,750
[music fades]

755
00:36:26,833 --> 00:36:29,040
YANG-DA MEDICAL SYSTEM: YEH HSIN-MEI

756
00:36:29,041 --> 00:36:30,499
[Geng-ming] "Injury assessment."

757
00:36:30,500 --> 00:36:33,166
"Alcohol poisoning and abortion."

758
00:36:36,375 --> 00:36:39,041
I really think
that Mrs. Yeh has had it tough.

759
00:36:39,958 --> 00:36:43,499
You know, Hsin-mei had different men
with her every time she came here.

760
00:36:43,500 --> 00:36:45,707
All three of her kids
are with different men.

761
00:36:45,708 --> 00:36:47,540
Since the grandkids came along,

762
00:36:47,541 --> 00:36:51,250
Mrs. Yeh has been selling vegetables
at the market to look after all of them.

763
00:36:52,166 --> 00:36:54,958
She hasn't had an easy life at all.

764
00:36:57,708 --> 00:36:59,040
Mrs. Yeh.

765
00:36:59,041 --> 00:37:00,665
Finished with the form?

766
00:37:00,666 --> 00:37:01,583
Yes.

767
00:37:03,083 --> 00:37:04,916
- [Hsiu-ju] Just have a seat here.
- [Mrs. Yeh] Sure.

768
00:37:05,541 --> 00:37:07,125
- Just... Here.
- Okay.

769
00:37:15,583 --> 00:37:16,999
Poor Hsin-mei.

770
00:37:17,000 --> 00:37:18,707
She never knew her father.

771
00:37:18,708 --> 00:37:21,333
That's why things turned out like this.

772
00:37:21,875 --> 00:37:23,666
[sobs softly] Maybe, this...

773
00:37:24,666 --> 00:37:26,291
It's a good thing.

774
00:37:26,791 --> 00:37:28,249
For Hsin-mei.

775
00:37:28,250 --> 00:37:29,916
[crying]

776
00:37:39,541 --> 00:37:41,375
Mrs. Yeh, what's on your arm?

777
00:37:43,583 --> 00:37:44,582
Oh, no.

778
00:37:44,583 --> 00:37:45,582
It's nothing.

779
00:37:45,583 --> 00:37:47,207
I... I'm fine.

780
00:37:47,208 --> 00:37:49,291
[breath trembling]

781
00:37:56,875 --> 00:37:58,250
[wailing] Hsin-mei.

782
00:38:00,083 --> 00:38:01,708
I failed you.

783
00:38:04,458 --> 00:38:05,957
Hsin-mei.

784
00:38:05,958 --> 00:38:07,040
[Geng-ming] <i>Dr. Chou?</i>

785
00:38:07,041 --> 00:38:09,500
I have some doubts about Hsin-mei's death.

786
00:38:10,416 --> 00:38:13,333
I saw Mrs. Yeh's arms have scratch marks.

787
00:38:13,958 --> 00:38:14,958
And look...

788
00:38:15,916 --> 00:38:18,457
Traces of blood under the fingernails.

789
00:38:18,458 --> 00:38:20,207
And there are marks on her neck.

790
00:38:20,208 --> 00:38:22,291
[foreboding music playing]

791
00:38:23,291 --> 00:38:24,750
Do you think that...

792
00:38:28,708 --> 00:38:29,791
Doctor?

793
00:38:31,833 --> 00:38:32,833
Doctor?

794
00:38:35,541 --> 00:38:37,458
Mrs. Yeh, don't leave just yet.

795
00:38:39,083 --> 00:38:40,083
Hsiu-ju.

796
00:38:40,958 --> 00:38:41,957
Call the police.

797
00:38:41,958 --> 00:38:43,749
- But she...
- Right now.

798
00:38:43,750 --> 00:38:44,832
Doctor.

799
00:38:44,833 --> 00:38:47,166
[phone vibrating]

800
00:38:47,666 --> 00:38:49,749
- Director. On my way.
- But...

801
00:38:49,750 --> 00:38:52,083
- I see. I'll be right over.
- Doctor. Uh...

802
00:38:53,500 --> 00:38:54,791
[sighs wearily]

803
00:38:59,666 --> 00:39:01,957
[Chia-hsin] Luckily,
the family seems more amenable,

804
00:39:01,958 --> 00:39:04,041
so there's a chance we can settle.

805
00:39:07,500 --> 00:39:09,249
[Cheng-chun] Director Chang,
you needed me?

806
00:39:09,250 --> 00:39:12,000
That's all for their mediations,
so I'll get going.

807
00:39:13,708 --> 00:39:15,208
How's your paper on the new drug?

808
00:39:16,750 --> 00:39:18,790
Uh... Everything's underway.

809
00:39:18,791 --> 00:39:20,833
That's great. You know, sometimes,

810
00:39:21,458 --> 00:39:23,749
we need a chance to recharge.

811
00:39:23,750 --> 00:39:25,999
PRESIDENT CHANG HSUEH-HUNG

812
00:39:26,000 --> 00:39:28,915
I can't make the show. You go for me.

813
00:39:28,916 --> 00:39:30,791
I've got two tickets here.

814
00:39:35,958 --> 00:39:37,540
Well, thank you.

815
00:39:37,541 --> 00:39:39,291
- Very thoughtful.
- [Hsueh-hung] Hmm.

816
00:39:47,166 --> 00:39:50,499
I just raised my suspicions,
and he went and called the police.

817
00:39:50,500 --> 00:39:51,665
[sighs]

818
00:39:51,666 --> 00:39:54,125
We've got no idea
if Hsin-mei's mom did it.

819
00:39:55,708 --> 00:39:57,374
I mean, how's she going to feel?

820
00:39:57,375 --> 00:39:59,208
How's she gonna face her grandchildren?

821
00:40:00,708 --> 00:40:03,583
[sighs wearily]
How will they ever get through this?

822
00:40:05,000 --> 00:40:06,874
I feel like our job is to treat patients

823
00:40:06,875 --> 00:40:08,874
and not get involved in anything else.

824
00:40:08,875 --> 00:40:12,333
We don't just treat patients,
we make decisions that affect their lives.

825
00:40:13,083 --> 00:40:15,083
You don't think Dr. Chou was too rash?

826
00:40:21,375 --> 00:40:23,333
- [woman] Sorry, I've got it somewhere.
- Thank you.

827
00:40:23,833 --> 00:40:25,500
[cashier] The total's 200.

828
00:40:26,958 --> 00:40:28,208
[Mrs. Chen] It's in here.

829
00:40:30,625 --> 00:40:32,290
- Two hundred?
- [cashier] Yes.

830
00:40:32,291 --> 00:40:34,165
- There.
- [cashier] Ah, thank you.

831
00:40:34,166 --> 00:40:35,666
[cash register beeps, clanks]

832
00:40:38,208 --> 00:40:39,040
Thank you.

833
00:40:39,041 --> 00:40:40,666
Oh, um...

834
00:40:42,000 --> 00:40:42,833
Mrs. Chen?

835
00:40:44,333 --> 00:40:45,332
How is your husband?

836
00:40:45,333 --> 00:40:46,915
I heard surgery went well.

837
00:40:46,916 --> 00:40:48,249
Has he woken up yet?

838
00:40:48,250 --> 00:40:50,416
Apparently, things are stable for now.

839
00:40:51,208 --> 00:40:55,541
But they still don't understand how a cold
could get so serious out of nowhere.

840
00:40:57,416 --> 00:41:00,874
Uh, thanks for paying for me.
I'll bring the money to the ER later.

841
00:41:00,875 --> 00:41:02,374
Oh, there's no need.

842
00:41:02,375 --> 00:41:04,457
Actually, the ice cream place here
is great.

843
00:41:04,458 --> 00:41:06,124
We could get some. Ah, Tung-yen--

844
00:41:06,125 --> 00:41:07,499
You know, we've been there.

845
00:41:07,500 --> 00:41:09,624
Whenever Chia-hao and I
were here for an appointment,

846
00:41:09,625 --> 00:41:11,165
we'd get some.

847
00:41:11,166 --> 00:41:14,499
But he had a toothache a while back,
so we never went again.

848
00:41:14,500 --> 00:41:16,332
We can get some when he's better.

849
00:41:16,333 --> 00:41:17,541
A tooth...

850
00:41:20,875 --> 00:41:22,207
Could that cause inflammation?

851
00:41:22,208 --> 00:41:23,665
It could.

852
00:41:23,666 --> 00:41:24,625
[gasps]

853
00:41:25,250 --> 00:41:27,749
Mrs. Chen! We know the cause
of your husband's fever.

854
00:41:27,750 --> 00:41:29,416
Tung-yen, ICU, come on!

855
00:41:39,041 --> 00:41:40,291
[knocks]

856
00:41:41,166 --> 00:41:42,582
You got a call from ICU?

857
00:41:42,583 --> 00:41:43,666
Hmm.

858
00:41:44,250 --> 00:41:45,582
Chen Chia-hao's infection.

859
00:41:45,583 --> 00:41:47,874
It was caused by pulpitis,
which led to pneumonia,

860
00:41:47,875 --> 00:41:49,833
which is why his condition worsened.

861
00:41:50,458 --> 00:41:51,500
Pulpitis?

862
00:41:52,833 --> 00:41:53,832
[sighs]

863
00:41:53,833 --> 00:41:55,832
Why didn't we notice that one?

864
00:41:55,833 --> 00:41:58,540
I heard Geng-ming
found out about it by accident

865
00:41:58,541 --> 00:42:00,875
after, uh, chatting with his wife.

866
00:42:02,041 --> 00:42:02,916
Hmm.

867
00:42:03,583 --> 00:42:04,540
[scoffs]

868
00:42:04,541 --> 00:42:06,124
Well, now I see why.

869
00:42:06,125 --> 00:42:08,249
You shocked everyone by choosing him.

870
00:42:08,250 --> 00:42:09,666
[both chuckle]

871
00:42:10,250 --> 00:42:14,583
By the way, I've heard there's been
a formal legal notice given.

872
00:42:15,083 --> 00:42:17,500
So you're not going to settle?

873
00:42:18,500 --> 00:42:21,082
Apparently, they want
the compensation increased.

874
00:42:21,083 --> 00:42:23,833
The point is,
they threatened Chiu and Hsiu-ju.

875
00:42:24,416 --> 00:42:25,833
Of course, I won't settle.

876
00:42:27,000 --> 00:42:28,915
Well, if I can help, let me know.

877
00:42:28,916 --> 00:42:29,833
I'm here.

878
00:42:30,666 --> 00:42:31,583
Hmm.

879
00:42:32,083 --> 00:42:34,457
I might head back.
Good luck with your paper.

880
00:42:34,458 --> 00:42:35,458
Mmm.

881
00:42:37,291 --> 00:42:38,125
Yu-hua.

882
00:42:40,791 --> 00:42:41,666
Um...

883
00:42:42,750 --> 00:42:43,583
So, when you...

884
00:42:44,458 --> 00:42:45,833
Uh, yesterday...

885
00:42:46,791 --> 00:42:48,958
[sighs] Forget it. Get on with your work.

886
00:42:53,625 --> 00:42:54,790
[sighs wearily]

887
00:42:54,791 --> 00:42:58,415
Oh, if you wanna know
what Dr. Huang and I did yesterday, we...

888
00:42:58,416 --> 00:42:59,665
worked out.

889
00:42:59,666 --> 00:43:02,125
[playful music playing]

890
00:43:02,833 --> 00:43:05,000
At the gym, we got sweaty.

891
00:43:05,500 --> 00:43:06,708
It felt good.

892
00:43:08,208 --> 00:43:09,207
[chuckles]

893
00:43:09,208 --> 00:43:11,291
[footsteps receding]

894
00:43:13,166 --> 00:43:14,791
They worked out?

895
00:43:17,375 --> 00:43:19,165
[man] I'll give these to you.

896
00:43:19,166 --> 00:43:21,208
- [Hsi] Just keep an eye on him.
- All right.

897
00:43:26,750 --> 00:43:28,082
Hey, where'd you go?

898
00:43:28,083 --> 00:43:30,166
- You disappeared.
- Mmm.

899
00:43:31,166 --> 00:43:32,707
We went to save a life.

900
00:43:32,708 --> 00:43:34,541
[laughs]

901
00:43:36,041 --> 00:43:38,166
[upbeat music playing]

902
00:43:39,041 --> 00:43:41,707
So, you're hanging out
with the weirdo now?

903
00:43:41,708 --> 00:43:44,875
His weirdness is kind of interesting,
don't you think?

904
00:43:52,333 --> 00:43:53,166
[Mrs. Chen] Doctor?

905
00:43:53,708 --> 00:43:55,583
- Oh, Mrs. Chen.
- Uh, hi.

906
00:43:56,791 --> 00:43:58,082
Well, my husband woke up.

907
00:43:58,083 --> 00:43:59,583
- Oh.
- [Mrs. Chen sighs]

908
00:44:00,166 --> 00:44:01,750
He wanted me to give you this.

909
00:44:06,375 --> 00:44:09,332
THANKS FOR SAVING MY LIFE

910
00:44:09,333 --> 00:44:11,083
Thank you so much.

911
00:44:17,083 --> 00:44:19,749
[officer] You'll need to come with me
and give a statement.

912
00:44:19,750 --> 00:44:22,166
[chattering indistinctly]

913
00:44:25,500 --> 00:44:26,499
[Mrs. Yeh groans]

914
00:44:26,500 --> 00:44:27,875
[officer] Are you okay?

915
00:44:28,791 --> 00:44:29,957
[Mrs. Yeh panting softly]

916
00:44:29,958 --> 00:44:31,375
[Cheng-chun] You think I'm heartless?

917
00:44:32,625 --> 00:44:33,500
Oh...

918
00:44:34,125 --> 00:44:35,875
No, of course not.

919
00:44:36,583 --> 00:44:39,999
I just worry about the kids
who've lost their mother.

920
00:44:40,000 --> 00:44:41,665
Now, their grandmother.

921
00:44:41,666 --> 00:44:42,582
It's very sad.

922
00:44:42,583 --> 00:44:44,915
What's an emergency physician's job?

923
00:44:44,916 --> 00:44:46,541
[inhales] It's to save lives.

924
00:44:48,791 --> 00:44:50,416
This is Mrs. Yeh's bag.

925
00:44:51,000 --> 00:44:52,458
Why do you think she has

926
00:44:53,166 --> 00:44:54,750
so much chocolate milk?

927
00:44:55,333 --> 00:44:56,625
And these? Hmm?

928
00:44:57,625 --> 00:44:59,083
Is that a sedative?

929
00:44:59,875 --> 00:45:01,374
Do you think it was for her grandkids?

930
00:45:01,375 --> 00:45:03,457
Our job is to save lives.

931
00:45:03,458 --> 00:45:06,249
But not just the ones
that come to ER, right?

932
00:45:06,250 --> 00:45:08,333
[melancholic music playing]

933
00:45:10,875 --> 00:45:11,875
[door clanks]

934
00:45:21,541 --> 00:45:23,541
[music continues playing]

935
00:45:44,666 --> 00:45:48,666
MISSING PERSON: CHOU CHENG-SIONG

936
00:45:50,208 --> 00:45:51,625
[sighs]

937
00:45:54,875 --> 00:45:55,790
Hi, excuse me.

938
00:45:55,791 --> 00:45:57,790
Can I ask you if you've seen this person?

939
00:45:57,791 --> 00:46:00,125
- Mmm, I haven't, no.
- Thank you.

940
00:46:00,750 --> 00:46:01,832
Hi, can I ask...

941
00:46:01,833 --> 00:46:03,832
if you've seen this person around?

942
00:46:03,833 --> 00:46:06,624
[man 1] That's the guy
who used to own the noodle place, right?

943
00:46:06,625 --> 00:46:08,666
Did he kill your family too?

944
00:46:10,000 --> 00:46:10,958
[sighs]

945
00:46:12,083 --> 00:46:13,999
[ominous music playing]

946
00:46:14,000 --> 00:46:16,083
[machine beeping]

947
00:46:17,750 --> 00:46:19,582
[doctor breathing shakily]

948
00:46:19,583 --> 00:46:20,583
[injection thuds]

949
00:46:21,916 --> 00:46:23,915
[doctor breathing heavily]

950
00:46:23,916 --> 00:46:25,416
DR. CHOU CHENG-CHUN

951
00:46:26,583 --> 00:46:28,374
[man shouting]
<i>You promised me you'd save him!</i>

952
00:46:28,375 --> 00:46:29,916
[Cheng-chun] <i>Actually, it's fair to say...</i>

953
00:46:30,833 --> 00:46:32,416
I killed his family.

954
00:46:38,375 --> 00:46:40,375
[closing theme music playing]
